            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> So after a lot of back and forth I decided to go ahead and replace `ignore_lines` with a more flexible `ignore_text` and `ignore_attr`. Both of new options can be either an array of number for lines to ignore text/attr _or_ a boolean indicating whether to ignore the whole part (for example, `ignore_attr = true` ignores any highlighting when comparing screenshots).\n> \n> The downside is that leaving `ignore_lines` felt redundant, so it is now soft deprecated. It will work at least until the next release (but with annoying warning) and will be removed some time afterwards. [@ibhagwan](https://github.com/ibhagwan), if anybody will complain about that, I'll tell them that it's your fault :)\n\nTysm @echasnovski, no problem I’ll take the blame :)\n\n@phanen, we probably have to change this too: https://github.com/ibhagwan/fzf-lua/commit/ea6d8ce0842c9a0d16587fcaaa75efe64e8c5695.",
            "created_at": "2025-05-30T13:01:48Z",
